   "type": "container-law",
   "text": "Arkansas Code § 8-6-418 (also AGFC Code 37.11): no glass containers within a vessel within the banks of navigable waterways. Anyone carrying food or drink in a canoe, kayak, inner tube or other easily-swamped vessel must keep it in sealed, sturdy containers, affix a closable trash container or bag (sturdy or mesh) to the vessel and carry trash out, and hold beverages in a floating holder. Fine up to $500 per violation.",
   "sourceName": "ar_code_8_6_418",
